articles, reports, and presentations—with care for readability, layout, and the integrity of your original content.</p>\n      <div class="hero-cta">\n        <a class="button button-primary" href="#install">Get started<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>\n        <a class="button" href="#concept">Learn more<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class="hero-foot"><span>OPEN SOURCE</span><span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>FOUR SKILLS</span><span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>TRADITIONAL CHINESE FIRST</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class="hero-stage" aria-label="KUMIHAN official logo">\n      <div class="logo-card"><img src="assets/KUMIHAN_OFFICIAL_LOGO_MASTER_20261014.png" width="1254" height="1254" alt="KUMIHAN official logo" fetchpriority="high"></div>\n      <div class="stage-label"><span lang="zh-Hant-TW">閱讀</span> — <span>HK: confirm the house style first</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="intro-strip" id="concept" aria-labelledby="concept-title">\n  <div class="shell intro-layout">\n    <div><span class="section-number">01 / THE IDEA</span></div>\n    <div class="intro-text"><h2 id="concept-title">Not a uniform look<br><em>the right form for each message</em></h2><p>Every brief, audience, and message is different. KUMIHAN｜字衡 helps AI shape typography, spacing, and hierarchy around the meaning and priorities of each piece—rather than applying one template to everything.</p></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="features" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">\n  <div class="shell">\n    <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-number">02 / WHAT MATTERS</div><h2 id="features-title">Four things worth getting right</h2></div><p>Practical priorities for creating and reviewing Traditional Chinese content.</p></div>\n    <div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature"><div class="feature-index">01 / REGION</div><div class="feature-motif" aria-hidden="true">「」</div><h3>Taiwan and Hong Kong in context</h3><p>Quotation, punctuation, glyphs and spacing are interpreted in regional and editorial context. Taiwan conventions are not silently imposed on Hong Kong.</p></article><article class="feature"><div class="feature-index">02 / STRUCTURE</div><div class="feature-motif" aria-hidden="true">▮▮▯</div><h3>Purposeful structure</h3><p>Shape the layout around the information, its priority, and the reader’s goal.</p></article><article class="feature"><div class="feature-index">03 / FIDELITY</div><div class="feature-motif" aria-hidden="true">臺 / 港</div><h3>Source fidelity</h3><p>Names, brands, prices, URLs, regional variants and Unicode sequences are never normalized merely to fit a layout.</p></article><article class="feature"><div class="feature-index">04 / REVIEW</div><div class="feature-motif" aria-hidden="true">◌</div><h3>Read-only review</h3><p>Check finished work and organize issues—without touching the files.</p></article></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="idea-band" id="regions" aria-labelledby="idea-title">\n  <div class="shell idea-layout locale-layout">\n    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="line" aria-hidden="true"></span> TAIWAN / HONG KONG</p><h2 id="idea-title">One writing system different editorial contexts</h2><p>In both regions the supplied code points are preserved. Actual glyphs and line breaks still require inspection in the target renderer.</p></div>\n    <div class="locale-cards"><article lang="zh-Hant-TW"><div class="locale-tag"><span lang="en">TW</span><strong lang="en">Taiwan</strong></div><code lang="en">zh-Hant-TW</code><p lang="en">For newly written prose, 「」 and nested 『』 are an initial recommendation—not a mandate for supplied quotations or every publisher. Punctuation squeezing is optional.</p></article><article lang="zh-Hant-HK"><div class="locale-tag"><span lang="en">HK</span><strong lang="en">Hong Kong</strong></div><code lang="en">zh-Hant-HK</code><p lang="en">First identify the publisher, institution or project house style for quotations, glyphs and punctuation. Taiwanese educational conventions are not the default.</p></article></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="skills-section" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title">\n  <div class="shell">\n    <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-number">03 / THE SKILLS</div><h2 id="skills-title">Four skills<br>One approach</h2></div><p>From scoping the work to web, documents, and review.</p></div>\n    <div class="skills-grid"><a class="skill-card" href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan/tree/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/skills/kumihan-ziheng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="card-top"><span class="skill-type">01 / ENTRY</span><span class="skill-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◆</span></div><div><h3 class="skill-name">kumihan-ziheng</h3><p class="skill-desc">Start here. Set the locale, medium and permitted change scope before design begins.</p><div class="skill-end"><span>View skill</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></div></a><a class="skill-card" href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan/tree/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/skills/kumihan-ziheng-web" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="card-top"><span class="skill-type">02 / WEB</span><span class="skill-symbol" aria-hidden="true">文</span></div><div><h3 class="skill-name">kumihan-ziheng-web</h3><p class="skill-desc">Typography and design for Traditional Chinese websites, articles, landing pages, and UI.</p><div class="skill-end"><span>View skill</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></div></a><a class="skill-card" href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan/tree/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/skills/kumihan-ziheng-documents" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="card-top"><span class="skill-type">03 / DOCUMENTS</span><span class="skill-symbol" aria-hidden="true">版</span></div><div><h3 class="skill-name">kumihan-ziheng-documents</h3><p class="skill-desc">Structure and readability for reports, business documents, and slide decks.</p><div class="skill-end"><span>View skill</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></div></a><a class="skill-card" href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan/tree/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/skills/kumihan-ziheng-review" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="card-top"><span class="skill-type">04 / REVIEW</span><span class="skill-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✓</span></div><div><h3 class="skill-name">kumihan-ziheng-review</h3><p class="skill-desc">Review typography, information, and layout without editing source files.</p><div class="skill-end"><span>View skill</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></div></a></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="install-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title"><!-- edition-version:install --><div class="edition-version" lang="en" data-edition-version="install" data-release-status="unpublished" dir="ltr"><strong>Source <bdi dir="ltr">v0.1.0</bdi></strong><span>Release unpublished — Published ZIP downloads unavailable</span></div><!-- /edition-version:install -->\n  <div class="shell install-layout">\n    <div class="install-intro"><div class="section-number">04 / GET STARTED</div><h2 id="install-title">Start with the AI tools<br>you already use</h2><p>Setup varies by tool. Pick the guide for yours, then choose the skills you need.</p></div>\n    <div><div class="install-links"><a class="platform-row" href="docs/install-ziheng.en.html"><span class="platform-index">01</span><div class="platform-info"><div class="platform-name">ChatGPT / Codex</div><div class="platform-note">Guides for adding skills, registering plugins, and local installation</div></div><span class="platform-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="platform-row" href="docs/install-ziheng-claude.en.html"><span class="platform-index">02</span><div class="platform-info"><div class="platform-name">Claude / Claude Code</div><div class="platform-note">Setup guide for Claude Code and Claude chat</div></div><span class="platform-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="platform-row" href="docs/install-ziheng-gemini.en.html"><span class="platform-index">03</span><div class="platform-info"><div class="platform-name">Gemini</div><div class="platform-note">Setup guide for Gemini CLI and the Gemini app</div></div><span class="platform-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="install-extra">You can also <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/landco-llc/kumihan/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/downloads/plugins/kumihan-ziheng-0.1.0.zip" download>download the ZIP<span lang="en"> (Source ZIP)</span></a> or view the source on <a href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan/tree/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.</div></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="status-section" aria-labelledby="status-title">\n  <div class="shell status-box">\n    <div><div class="status-title" id="status-title">VERSION / v0.1.0</div><p><strong>Clear verification boundaries</strong></p><p>ZiHeng includes 15 regional rules, 16 shared policies and four skills. Only limited static checks are automated; browser layout, Office/PDF rendering and host behavior are not universally verified. The v0.2.0 source candidate separates register, element role, source permissions and evidence. Its 32 case definitions are separate from rendered, interaction and native-language acceptance. Shared version display awaits integration; older downloads remain available.</p></div>\n    <div class="status-meta"><a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/landco-llc/kumihan/main/plugins/kumihan-ziheng/downloads/plugins/kumihan-ziheng-0.1.0.zip" download>Download latest ↗<span lang="en"> (Source ZIP)</span></a><br>OPEN SOURCE · APACHE 2.0</div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="cta-section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">\n  <div class="shell cta-layout">\n    <div><h2 id="cta-title">Another way to design<br>in Traditional Chinese</h2><p>KUMIHAN｜字衡 is open source. The skills, releases, and full change history are on GitHub.</p></div>\n    <a class="button" href="https://github.com/landco-llc/kumihan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on GitHub<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>\n  </div>\n</section>\n</main>\n<footer class="kumihan-footer"><div class="kf-inner"><div class="kf-brand"><div class="kf-mark">KUMIHAN</div><p class="kf-note">Open-source typography &amp; design guidance by <a href="https://landco.co.jp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">L&amp;Co. LLC</a>.</p></div><nav class="kf-links" aria-label="KUMIHAN"><a href="index.html">KUMIHAN</a><details class="kf-menu"><summary>Choose a language</summary><ul><li><a href="kumihan-ar.en.html"><span class="code">AR</span> - Arabic</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-bn.en.html"><span class="code">BN</span> - Bangla</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-de.en.html"><span class="code">DE</span> - German</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-es.en.html"><span class="code">ES</span> - Spanish</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-fa.en.html"><span class="code">FA</span> - Persian</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-fr.en.html"><span class="code">FR</span> - French</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-hi.en.html"><span class="code">HI</span> - Hindi</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-id.en.html"><span class="code">ID</span> - Indonesian</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-it.en.html"><span class="code">IT</span> - Italian</a></li><li><a href="en.html"><span class="code">JA</span> - Japanese</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-km.en.html"><span class="code">KM</span> - Khmer</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-ko.en.html"><span class="code">KO</span> - Korean</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-pl.en.html"><span class="code">PL</span> - Polish</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-pt.en.html"><span class="code">PT</span> - Portuguese</a></li><li><a href="kumihan-ru.en.html"><span class="code">RU</span> - Russian</a></li><li><a href="kumi